CLR (rocclr) D2H copy routing (gfx803): never write a pinned or
registered/locked host buffer directly from the copy engine -- force the
GPU-staging path (GPU staging buffer + CPU memcpy) for D2H copies.

WHY
---
torch `.cpu()`/`.to('cpu')` D2H copies under alloc/free churn fault on
gfx803 (7.14 and 10.0 alike, same torch 2.13) with "Memory access fault
... Page not present" (write from TC). Root cause: the copy engine
(blit/copy shader or SDMA) writes the pinned/registered host destination
directly, and on gfx803 the engine's stores to host memory drain from L2
to the host buffer only after the copy's completion -- a system-scope
release fence does not change that on this hardware. The write-back
therefore races the host buffer's unlock/teardown and faults on the
removed mapping.

Isolation: the fault needs a D2H copy into host memory under churn.
A plain compute kernel writing the same registered host buffer is clean
(scalar and vectorized stores), so it is specifically the copy engine's
host write. Disabling host pinning (GPU_PINNED_MIN_XFER_SIZE huge /
GPU_PINNED_XFER_SIZE=0) forces the staging path and the fault disappears;
the pinned path faults 5/5 with both the shader copy (HSA_ENABLE_SDMA=0)
and the SDMA copy (GPU_FORCE_BLIT_COPY_SIZE=0). Minimal repro:
hipHostRegister a pageable buffer, hipMemcpy D2H into it, unregister,
repeated with device alloc/free churn -- faults within a few rounds,
fault address inside the registered buffer's GPUVM mapping.

WHAT
---
Force the existing GPU-staging D2H path for all copies whose destination
is host memory:

- DmaBlitManager::readBuffer and KernelBlitManager::readBuffer: pass
  kEnablePin=false to getBuffer so a pageable destination is copied into a
  GPU staging buffer and landed by the CPU memcpy, never written directly
  by the copy engine.
- submitReadMemory (ReadMemoryCommand): when the destination resolves to a
  registered/locked host buffer (hostMemory != nullptr), route through the
  staged readBuffer instead of the accelerated copyBuffer.
- copyMemory (CopyMemoryCommand): when the destination is
  host-memory-direct-access, route through the staged readBuffer instead of
  copyBuffer.

The staging path is the same one the codebase already falls back to, and
is correct on this hardware: the GPU writes its own staging buffer (whose
mapping the fmm keeps alive) and the CPU memcpy lands the data, so no
engine write is ever outstanding against the host buffer's lifetime. This
costs an extra copy, which is the correct trade -- the direct host write
is broken on gfx803.

Applies AFTER graph-replay-batch-chunk-deadlock.patch (the rocvirtual.cpp
hunk offsets assume its chunk-size change is present).

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE against 10.0 -- source applies and
reads correctly, but the D2H churn repro has not been re-run against a
rebuild with this hunk yet.
diff --git a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
--- a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
@@ -52,7 +52,12 @@ bool DmaBlitManager::readBuffer(device::Memory& srcMemory, void* dstHost,
     const_address addrSrc = gpuMem(srcMemory).getDeviceMemory() + origin[0];
     address addrDst = reinterpret_cast<address>(dstHost);
     constexpr bool kHostToDev = false;
-    constexpr bool kEnablePin = true;
+    // GFX803: never pin the host destination for a D2H copy -- the copy
+    // engine's stores to a pinned host buffer drain from L2 after the copy
+    // completes and fault once the pin is unlocked (page not present, write
+    // from TC). Force the GPU-staging path: the copy writes a GPU staging
+    // buffer and the CPU memcpy below lands the data.
+    constexpr bool kEnablePin = false;
     if (!hsaCopyStagedOrPinned(addrSrc, addrDst, copySize, kHostToDev, copyMetadata, kEnablePin)) {
       LogError("DmaBlitManager:: readBuffer copy failure!");
       return false;
@@ -2155,7 +2160,9 @@ bool KernelBlitManager::readBuffer(device::Memory& srcMemory, void* dstHost,
 
       while (totalSize > 0) {
         BufferState outBuffer = {0};
-        constexpr bool kEnablePin = true;
+        // GFX803: never pin the host destination for a D2H copy (see
+        // DmaBlitManager::readBuffer); force the GPU-staging path.
+        constexpr bool kEnablePin = false;
         constexpr bool kFirstTx = false;
         getBuffer(static_cast<const_address>(dstAddr + stagedCopyOffset), totalSize, kEnablePin,
                   kFirstTx, outBuffer);
diff --git a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
